searchData={"items":[{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedEx\n\nMedEx is an Elixir SDK for recording clinical audio and streaming an independent\nlive WebRTC Opus preview. It accepts indexed mono 48 kHz signed PCM16LE audio,\nwrites an immutable content-addressed WAV artifact, and encodes live Opus for a\nreplaceable WebRTC listener. The host application owns authorization, signaling,\nand clinical review.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Overview","doc":"Add `:med_ex` to your list of dependencies in `mix.exs`:\n\n```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:med_ex, \"~> 0.1.0\"}\n  ]\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites - Overview","doc":"- Elixir `~> 1.20` (tested on Elixir `1.20.5` / OTP `29.1.2`).\n- On Ubuntu 26.04, native WebRTC dependencies (`ex_dtls`, `ex_libsrtp`) require a\n  C compiler, `make`, `pkg-config`, and OpenSSL development headers\n  (`build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev`).\n- Live Opus encoding uses `membrane_opus_plugin`, which downloads precompiled\n  `libopus` binaries on supported Linux/macOS targets and falls back to system\n  `libopus-dev` (`pkg-config`) when building from source.","ref":"readme.html#prerequisites"},{"type":"extras","title":"Quick example - Overview","doc":"```elixir\n# Start a capture under your host DynamicSupervisor (owner is the producer PID)\n{:ok, capture} =\n  DynamicSupervisor.start_child(\n    MyApp.Captures,\n    {MedEx.Capture, owner: self(), acquisition_id: \"acq-1\", artifact_dir: \"/var/lib/myapp/wavs\"}\n  )\n\n# Push contiguous 20 ms chunks (960 mono samples = 1,920 PCM16LE bytes at 48 kHz)\n:ok = MedEx.Capture.push(capture, 0, pcm_chunk_0)\n:ok = MedEx.Capture.push(capture, 960, pcm_chunk_1)\n\n# Finalize to an immutable \" .wav\" file and %MedEx.Evidence{}\n{:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{artifact_key: key, file_sha256: sha, sample_count: 1920}} =\n  MedEx.Capture.finish(capture)\n```","ref":"readme.html#quick-example"},{"type":"extras","title":"Scope in 0.1.0 - Overview","doc":"- **Supported audio profile:** Mono 48 kHz signed PCM16LE (up to 30 minutes per\n  capture) with independent send-only WebRTC Opus preview and packaged browser\n  capture/preview JS assets (`MedEx.Web.asset_path/1`).\n- **Out of scope in 0.1.0:** Video tracks, multi-channel ECG/PPG waveforms,\n  bundled TURN servers, clinical persistence, and FHIR export.","ref":"readme.html#scope-in-0-1-0"},{"type":"extras","title":"Guides - Overview","doc":"- [Host integration](guides/host_integration.md) — Elixir capture/preview\n  supervision, Phoenix signaling channel, binary PCM WebSocket contract, and\n  browser hook / AudioWorklet setup.\n- [Architecture and roadmap](guides/architecture_and_roadmap.md) — Capture vs.\n  preview failure domains, shipped vs. planned capabilities, and future\n  integrations.\n- [Source development](guides/source_development.md) — Working in the source\n  monorepo checkout and preparing Weld release bundles.","ref":"readme.html#guides"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Overview","doc":"Released under the MIT License.","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Host integration","doc":"# Host integration\n\nThis guide covers everything a Phoenix or Elixir host needs to capture indexed\nmono PCM16LE audio with `MedEx.Capture`, stream an independent live Opus preview\nover `MedEx.Preview`, and serve MedEx's packaged browser helpers.","ref":"host_integration.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites - Host integration","doc":"- Elixir `~> 1.20` (tested on Elixir `1.20.5` / OTP `29.1.2`).\n- Ubuntu 26.04 native build packages for WebRTC (`ex_dtls`, `ex_libsrtp`):\n  `build-essential`, `pkg-config`, and `libssl-dev`.\n- Live Opus encoding uses `membrane_opus_plugin`, which uses precompiled\n  `libopus` binaries on supported Linux/macOS targets (install `libopus-dev` if\n  compiling `libopus` from source).\n- Browser microphone capture (`getUserMedia` + `AudioWorklet`) requires a secure\n  context (`https://`, or `http://localhost` / `http://127.0.0.1` for local dev).","ref":"host_integration.html#prerequisites"},{"type":"extras","title":"1. Serve the packaged browser assets - Host integration","doc":"`MedEx.Web.asset_path/1` resolves the three JavaScript files shipped inside\n`:med_ex`:\n\n- `\"session_hook.js\"` — LiveView hook helper (`createMedExHook/1`) for the\n  clinician's receive-only WebRTC preview.\n- `\"pcm_capture.js\"` — patient-browser capture helper (`startPCM/4`).\n- `\"pcm_worklet.js\"` — `AudioWorkletProcessor` (`\"med-ex-indexed-pcm\"`) loaded\n  by `startPCM/4`.\n\nServe all three as `application/javascript` from your endpoint:\n\n```elixir\ndefp serve_med_ex_assets(%Plug.Conn{path_info: [\"med_ex\", name]} = conn, _opts)\n     when name in ~w(session_hook.js pcm_capture.js pcm_worklet.js) do\n  conn\n  |> Plug.Conn.put_resp_content_type(\"application/javascript\")\n  |> Plug.Conn.send_file(200, MedEx.Web.asset_path(name))\n  |> Plug.Conn.halt()\nend\n\ndefp serve_med_ex_assets(conn, _opts), do: conn\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#1-serve-the-packaged-browser-assets"},{"type":"extras","title":"2. Supervise live capture in your host - Host integration","doc":"Start a host-owned `DynamicSupervisor` (and optionally a `Registry` if preview\nchannels need to look up active captures by encounter). MedEx starts no global\ncapture processes.\n\n```elixir\n# In your application supervision tree:\nchildren = [\n  {Registry, keys: :unique, name: MyApp.ActiveCapture},\n  {DynamicSupervisor, strategy: :one_for_one, name: MyApp.Captures}\n]\n```\n\nFor the preview example below, start `{Phoenix.PubSub, name: MyApp.PubSub}`\nin the host supervisor as well. Register the encounter in `MyApp.ActiveCapture`\nfrom the producer process and broadcast after the capture starts.\n\nEach capture process takes `:owner`, `:acquisition_id`, and `:artifact_dir`:\n\n```elixir\n{:ok, _} = Registry.register(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id, nil)\n\n{:ok, capture} =\n  DynamicSupervisor.start_child(\n    MyApp.Captures,\n    {MedEx.Capture,\n     owner: self(),\n     acquisition_id: acquisition_id,\n     artifact_dir: artifact_dir}\n  )\n\nRegistry.update_value(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id, fn _ -> capture end)\nPhoenix.PubSub.broadcast(MyApp.PubSub, \"preview:\" <> encounter_id, {:capture_started, capture})\n```\n\n`MedEx.Capture` monitors `:owner` and aborts (deleting its temporary `.part`\nfile) if `:owner` exits before `finish/1`.","ref":"host_integration.html#2-supervise-live-capture-in-your-host"},{"type":"extras","title":"Handling binary PCM WebSocket frames - Host integration","doc":"In your authenticated WebSocket handler (e.g. a `WebSock` module), decode each\nbinary frame as an 8-byte unsigned big-endian starting sample index followed by\nPCM16LE bytes, push to `MedEx.Capture.push/3`, and reply with text `\"ack\"`:\n\n```elixir\ndef handle_in({< >, [opcode: :binary]}, state) do\n  case MedEx.Capture.push(state.capture, index, pcm) do\n    :ok -> {:push, {:text, \"ack\"}, state}\n    {:error, _reason} -> {:stop, :normal, 1008, {:text, \"invalid_capture\"}, state}\n  end\nend\n\ndef handle_in({\"finish\", [opcode: :text]}, state) do\n  case MedEx.Capture.finish(state.capture) do\n    {:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{} = evidence} ->\n      # Persist finalized evidence before closing the socket.\n      :ok = MyApp.ClinicalStore.record_ready(state.encounter_id, evidence)\n      {:stop, :normal, 1000, {:text, \"ready\"}, state}\n\n    {:error, _reason} ->\n      {:stop, :normal, 1011, {:text, \"capture_failed\"}, state}\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#handling-binary-pcm-websocket-frames"},{"type":"extras","title":"Capture rules and error returns - Host integration","doc":"| Rule / Operation | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sample format | Mono 48 kHz signed 16-bit little-endian PCM (`PCM16LE`). |\n| Frame size | Even byte count in `2..1920` (up to 960 samples / 20 ms). Only one short tail frame (`< 1920` bytes) is allowed, immediately before `finish/1`. |\n| Contiguity & limit | `first_sample` must start at `0` and advance contiguously without gaps, up to 30 minutes (`86_400_000` samples). Violations return `{:error, :invalid_frame}` and stop the capture. |\n| `finish/1` | Returns `{:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{}}`, `{:error, :empty_capture}` (0 samples pushed), `{:error, :artifact_conflict}` (existing file digest mismatch), or `{:error, posix}`. |\n| Preview fan-out | Only full 1,920-byte frames are offered to the preview encoder. Preview lag, drop, or encoder exit never blocks or aborts WAV capture. |\n\n### `MedEx.Evidence` fields\n\n`MedEx.Capture.finish/1` returns `%MedEx.Evidence{}`:\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `:acquisition_id` | Host-provided acquisition ID string |\n| `:artifact_key` | Content-addressed filename (`\" .wav\"`) |\n| `:file_sha256` | Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the complete WAV file |\n| `:pcm_sha256` | Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the raw PCM16LE bytes |\n| `:kind` | `:audio_pcm16_wav` |\n| `:sample_rate_hz` | `48_000` |\n| `:first_sample` | `0` (inclusive) |\n| `:end_sample` | Exclusive ending sample index |\n| `:sample_count` | Total captured mono samples |\n| `:continuity` | `:observed_continuous` |","ref":"host_integration.html#capture-rules-and-error-returns"},{"type":"extras","title":"3. Wire the preview signaling channel - Host integration","doc":"The clinician's Phoenix Channel owns one replaceable `MedEx.Preview` peer.\n`MedEx.Preview.answer/2` sends `{:ex_webrtc, peer.pid, {:connection_state_change, state}}`\nmessages to the channel process. Once `:connected`, subscribe the channel to\nthe active `MedEx.Capture` (only one subscriber is active at a time; a newer\nsubscriber replaces the previous one).\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyAppWeb.PreviewChannel do\n  use Phoenix.Channel\n\n  alias MedEx.{Capture, Preview}\n\n  @impl true\n  def join(\"signaling:\" <> encounter_id, %{\"connection_id\" => id}, socket)\n      when is_binary(id) do\n    # Authorize socket.assigns here before allowing join.\n    {:ok, %{session_id: encounter_id},\n     assign(socket,\n       encounter_id: encounter_id,\n       peer: nil,\n       capture: nil,\n       sequence: 0,\n       clock: nil,\n       connected: false\n     )}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_in(\"offer\", %{\"sdp\" => sdp}, %{assigns: %{peer: nil}} = socket) do\n    opts = [ice_servers: Application.get_env(:my_app, :ice_servers, [])]\n\n    case Preview.answer(sdp, opts) do\n      {:ok, peer, answer_sdp} ->\n        {:reply, {:ok, %{sdp: answer_sdp}}, assign(socket, :peer, peer)}\n\n      {:error, _reason} ->\n        {:reply, {:error, %{reason: \"negotiation_failed\"}}, socket}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info(\n        {:ex_webrtc, pid, {:connection_state_change, :connected}},\n        %{assigns: %{peer: %{pid: pid}, connected: false}} = socket\n      ) do\n    encounter_id = socket.assigns.encounter_id\n    :ok = Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(MyApp.PubSub, \"preview:\" <> encounter_id)\n\n    case Registry.lookup(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id) do\n      [{_producer, capture}] when is_pid(capture) -> send(self(), {:capture_started, capture})\n      _ -> :ok\n    end\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, :connected, true)}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:capture_started, capture}, %{assigns: %{connected: true}} = socket) do\n    case Capture.subscribe(capture) do\n      :ok ->\n        {:noreply, assign(socket, :capture, capture)}\n\n      {:error, :preview_unavailable} ->\n        push(socket, \"preview_failed\", %{})\n        {:noreply, socket}\n    end\n  catch\n    :exit, _ -> {:noreply, socket}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info(\n        {:med_ex_preview, capture, sample_index, packet},\n        %{assigns: %{capture: capture, peer: peer, sequence: seq, clock: clock}} = socket\n      ) do\n    tick = next_tick(clock, capture, sample_index)\n    :ok = Preview.send_opus(peer, packet, seq, tick)\n    :ok = Capture.demand(capture)\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, sequence: seq + 1, clock: {capture, sample_index, tick})}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:med_ex_preview_failed, capture, _reason}, %{assigns: %{capture: capture}} = socket) do\n    push(socket, \"preview_failed\", %{})\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, :capture, nil)}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info(\n        {:ex_webrtc, pid, {:connection_state_change, state}},\n        %{assigns: %{peer: %{pid: pid}}} = socket\n      )\n      when state in [:failed, :closed],\n      do: {:stop, :normal, socket}\n\n  def handle_info(_msg, socket), do: {:noreply, socket}\n\n  @impl true\n  def terminate(_reason, socket) do\n    if peer = socket.assigns[:peer], do: Preview.close(peer)\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  # Keep RTP media timestamps monotonic if a new capture starts on the same peer.\n  defp next_tick(nil, _capture, index), do: index\n  defp next_tick({capture, last, tick}, capture, index), do: tick + index - last\n  defp next_tick({_prev, _last, tick}, _capture, _index), do: tick + 960\nend\n```\n\nPass `:ice_servers` to `MedEx.Preview.answer/2` and `iceServers` to\n`createMedExHook/1` for host-managed STUN/TURN configuration. The default `[]`\nuses direct local candidates.","ref":"host_integration.html#3-wire-the-preview-signaling-channel"},{"type":"extras","title":"4. Browser preview hook (session_hook.js) - Host integration","doc":"Wrap the clinician preview controls in a LiveView container with\n**`phx-update=\"ignore\"`** (required so LiveView DOM diffs do not tear down the\nactive ` ` stream), `data-token` (sent in Phoenix Socket params), an\n` ` element, and an optional `[role=\"status\"]` element:\n\n```heex\n \n   Play preview \n   Disconnect \n   Reconnect \n    \n   idle \n \n```\n\nRegister the hook on your `LiveSocket`:\n\n```js\nimport { Socket } from \"/assets/phoenix.mjs\";\nimport { LiveSocket } from \"/assets/phoenix_live_view.esm.js\";\nimport { createMedExHook } from \"/med_ex/session_hook.js\";\n\nconst csrfToken = document.querySelector('meta[name=\"csrf-token\"]').content;\nconst liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n  params: { _csrf_token: csrfToken },\n  hooks: {\n    MedExSessionHook: createMedExHook({\n      Socket,\n      socketPath: \"/socket\",\n      topic: el => \"signaling:\" + el.dataset.encounterId,\n      play: \"#preview-play\",\n      disconnect: \"#preview-disconnect\",\n      reconnect: \"#preview-reconnect\",\n      iceServers: []\n    })\n  }\n});\nliveSocket.connect();\n```\n\nChannel protocol expected by `createMedExHook`:\n\n1. Joins `topic(el)` with `{ connection_id: crypto.randomUUID() }`, expecting\n   `{ session_id }`.\n2. Gathers browser ICE candidates and pushes `\"offer\"` with `{ sdp }`, expecting\n   `{ sdp }` answer.\n3. Handles server-pushed `\"preview_failed\"` by closing the peer cleanly and\n   displaying a retry status without affecting capture.","ref":"host_integration.html#4-browser-preview-hook-session_hook-js"},{"type":"extras","title":"5. Browser live PCM capture (pcm_capture.js & pcm_worklet.js) - Host integration","doc":"Call `startPCM` from a user gesture, such as clicking Start. Provide separate\nbuttons with IDs `finish-capture` and `abort-capture`. Enable Finish from the\nrecording callback once the server acknowledges the first frame.\n\n```js\nimport { startPCM } from \"/med_ex/pcm_capture.js\";\n\nconst socket = new WebSocket(\"wss://example.test/pcm\");\nawait new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n  socket.onopen = resolve;\n  socket.onerror = reject;\n  socket.onclose = reject;\n});\n\nconst handle = await startPCM(\n  socket,\n  \"/med_ex/pcm_worklet.js\",\n  outcome => console.log(\"Capture ended:\", outcome),\n  () => console.log(\"Recording active (first frame acknowledged)\")\n);\n\n// Use separate buttons for the two terminal actions.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#finish-capture\").onclick = () => handle.finish();\ndocument.querySelector(\"#abort-capture\").onclick = () => handle.abort();\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#5-browser-live-pcm-capture-pcm_capture-js-pcm_worklet-js"},{"type":"extras","title":"Live PCM wire protocol and outcome codes - Host integration","doc":"- **Audio constraints:** `AudioContext({ sampleRate: 48000 })` (fails with\n  `\"setup_failed\"` if the browser context cannot run at 48 kHz) and\n  `getUserMedia` with `channelCount: { exact: 1 }` and `echoCancellation`,\n  `noiseSuppression`, and `autoGainControl` set to `{ exact: false }`.\n- **Binary frames:** 8-byte unsigned big-endian `first_sample` index followed by\n  up to 960 mono `PCM16LE` samples (1,920 bytes).\n- **Flow control:** The worklet starts with 8 in-flight frame credits. The host\n  must reply with text `\"ack\"` after accepting each frame. After the first\n  `\"ack\"`, `startPCM/4` invokes `onRecording()`.\n- **Normal finish:** `handle.finish()` drains any final partial frame, sends\n  text `\"finish\"`, and waits for the host's terminal text frame (for example\n  `\"ready\"` or `\"capture_failed\"`).\n- **Startup & gap rules:** Allow up to 1 second for continuous microphone\n  startup (`\"capture_source_timeout\"` if no samples arrive). Any source gap\n  after the first frame ends capture with `\"capture_gap\"`.\n\nTerminal strings delivered to `onOutcome(outcome)`:\n\n| Outcome | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| Host text frame (e.g. `\"ready\"`, `\"capture_failed\"`, `\"invalid_capture\"`) | Any non-`\"ack\"` text message sent by the host closes capture with that string. |\n| `\"setup_failed\"` | Microphone permission/constraints, 48 kHz context, worklet load, or socket pre-check failed (`startPCM/4` also rejects). |\n| `\"capture_source_timeout\"` | No audio samples arrived within 1 second of start or during an empty-input stall. |\n| `\"capture_gap\"` | AudioWorklet detected a discontinuity in `currentFrame` after capture became active. |\n| `\"capture_overflow\"` | All 8 in-flight frame credits were exhausted without host `\"ack\"` replies. |\n| `\"source_ended\"` | Browser media track ended unexpectedly. |\n| `\"disconnected\"` | WebSocket closed or errored before a terminal host outcome arrived. |\n| `\"aborted\"` | Host browser code called `handle.abort()`. |","ref":"host_integration.html#live-pcm-wire-protocol-and-outcome-codes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Architecture and roadmap","doc":"# Architecture and roadmap\n\nMedEx provides real-time clinical media capture and WebRTC preview transport for\nElixir applications. Host applications own authorization, encounter state,\nclinician review, persistence, and healthcare record export—MedEx has no\ndatabase, Phoenix server, or FHIR dependency.","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Why two separate media paths? - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"Clinical diagnostic audio (such as remote auscultation) has conflicting\nrequirements:\n\n- **Live listening** needs low-latency, resilient WebRTC Opus streaming that can\n  drop packets or reconnect peers across network hiccups.\n- **Authoritative recording** needs bit-exact, continuous, lossless PCM audio\n  whose integrity is never compromised by WebRTC jitter, Opus compression, or\n  clinician browser disconnects.\n\nMedEx enforces this split in its process boundaries: live indexed PCM enters\n`MedEx.Capture`, which writes the lossless WAV directly and fans full 20 ms\nframes out to a bounded, disposable preview branch (`Membrane.Opus.Encoder`\nkept private behind `MedEx.Capture` → `MedEx.Preview` over `ExWebRTC`).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  PCM[\"Indexed PCM16LE (48 kHz)\"] --> Capture[\"MedEx.Capture (Lossless Writer)\"]\n  Capture --> WAV[\"Immutable &lt;sha256&gt;.wav + MedEx.Evidence\"]\n  Capture -. \"bounded 1-frame demand\" .-> Encoder[\"Private Membrane Opus Encoder\"]\n  Encoder --> Peer[\"MedEx.Preview (ExWebRTC)\"]\n  Peer --> Listener[\"Clinician Browser (Replaceable)\"]\n```","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#why-two-separate-media-paths"},{"type":"extras","title":"Process ownership and failure domains - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"| Component | Owner | Failure behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `MedEx.Capture` | Host `DynamicSupervisor` (`restart: :temporary`, no global names) | Monitors the `:owner` producer PID; aborts and deletes its `.part` file if the producer exits before `finish/1`. |\n| Preview encoder pipeline | Private to `MedEx.Capture` (`Membrane.Opus.Encoder`, `application: :audio`) | Isolated via trapped exits; if the encoder exits, capture notifies the subscriber with `{:med_ex_preview_failed, pid, reason}` and keeps recording. |\n| `MedEx.Preview` peer | Host signaling channel process | Peer drop, disconnect, or replacement only changes the preview subscriber; capture continues uninterrupted. |\n| `MedEx.Evidence` | Returned to host on `finish/1` | Carries `kind: :audio_pcm16_wav`, content-addressed `artifact_key`, separate `file_sha256` and `pcm_sha256`, sample bounds, and continuity verdict. |","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#process-ownership-and-failure-domains"},{"type":"extras","title":"Shipped in 0.1.0 vs. planned roadmap - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"| Capability | Status | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Indexed mono 48 kHz PCM16LE capture → immutable WAV + `MedEx.Evidence` | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Capture`, `MedEx.Evidence`, 30-minute cap, strict contiguity enforcement. |\n| Bounded live Opus encoding + replaceable send-only WebRTC preview | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Preview` (`ExWebRTC` + `ExRTP`), host-configurable `:ice_servers`, private `Membrane.Opus.Encoder`. |\n| Browser AudioWorklet PCM capture & LiveView preview hook assets | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Web.asset_path/1` (`session_hook.js`, `pcm_capture.js`, `pcm_worklet.js`). |\n| Hardware / gateway PCM sources (USB stethoscopes, BLE gateways) | **Planned** | Feed the same `MedEx.Capture.push/3` indexed PCM contract once a named device is verified end-to-end. |\n| Non-audio modalities (multi-channel ECG/PPG waveforms, video tracks) | **Planned** | Will define modality-specific capture and evidence contracts alongside `kind: :audio_pcm16_wav` rather than overloading PCM audio fields. |\n| Out-of-band signal analysis & inference workers (NeuroKit2, WFDB-Python, ONNX, voice AI) | **Planned** | Separately installed/deployed packages or workers consuming finalized `MedEx.Evidence` outside capture and emitting derived results with source digest and algorithm provenance. |\n| Multiparty SFU topologies (e.g. LiveKit) & managed TURN deployments | **Planned** | External media services integrated when a product topology requires multiparty forwarding or NAT relay. |\n\nSee [Host integration](host_integration.md) for the current SDK contract.","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#shipped-in-0-1-0-vs-planned-roadmap"},{"type":"extras","title":"Source development","doc":"# Source development\n\nThese instructions apply to the source repository checkout at\n . They are not needed when installing\n`:med_ex` as a Hex dependency.","ref":"source_development.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Repository layout - Source development","doc":"| Path | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `core/med_rtc` | `MedEx.Capture`, `MedEx.Evidence`, `MedEx.Preview`, WAV writer, and private Membrane Opus encoder. |\n| `core/med_web` | `MedEx.Web` asset locator and browser JS (`session_hook.js`, `pcm_capture.js`, `pcm_worklet.js`). |\n| `build_support/weld.exs` | Weld manifest projecting `core/med_rtc` and `core/med_web` into the single `:med_ex` Hex package. |\n| `dist/release_bundles/` | Gitignored output directory where `mix weld.release.prepare` writes the generated `project/`, rendered `docs/`, and `.tar` archive. |","ref":"source_development.html#repository-layout"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites (Ubuntu 26.04) - Source development","doc":"Install system packages:\n\n```sh\nsudo apt-get install -y git curl tar build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev\n```\n\n*(Install `libopus-dev` as well if compiling `membrane_opus_plugin` from source\ninstead of using precompiled binaries.)*\n\nActivate the exact Erlang and Elixir versions pinned in `.tool-versions`\n(`erlang 29.1.2`, `elixir 1.20.5-otp-29`) via `asdf` or `mise`.","ref":"source_development.html#prerequisites-ubuntu-26-04"},{"type":"extras","title":"Build, test, and prepare a release bundle - Source development","doc":"```sh\n./onboard.sh\nmix ci\nmix weld.release.prepare\n```\n\n`mix weld.release.prepare` prints the path to the generated bundle under\n`dist/release_bundles/med_ex/ - /`, containing:\n\n- `project/` — standalone generated `:med_ex` Mix project (can be referenced as\n  a local path dependency before Hex publication, or tested directly via\n  `mix deps.get && mix test`).\n- `docs/` — rendered ExDoc HTML preview (`docs/index.html`).\n- `med_ex- .tar` — exact Hex archive.\n- `release.json` — source revision, verification checks, and SHA-256 digests.","ref":"source_development.html#build-test-and-prepare-a-release-bundle"},{"type":"extras","title":"MedRTC","doc":"# med_rtc\n\nInternal media capture and WebRTC transport package for [MedEx](../../README.md).\n\nProvides `MedEx.Capture` (indexed 48 kHz mono PCM16LE WAV writer with bounded\nlive `Membrane.Opus.Encoder` preview fan-out), `MedEx.Evidence` (finalized\nartifact struct), and `MedEx.Preview` (replaceable send-only `ExWebRTC` peer).\nProjected with `core/med_web` into the single `:med_ex` Hex package.","ref":"med_rtc.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"MedWeb","doc":"# med_web\n\nInternal browser assets package for [MedEx](../../README.md).\n\nProvides `MedEx.Web.asset_path/1` to locate the three packaged JavaScript assets\n(`session_hook.js`, `pcm_capture.js`, and `pcm_worklet.js`) for LiveView preview\nsignaling and browser `AudioWorklet` PCM16LE capture. Projected with\n`core/med_rtc` into the single `:med_ex` Hex package.","ref":"med_web.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"0.1.0 - Changelog","doc":"- Record indexed browser PCM as content-addressed WAV evidence.\n- Encode live Opus on a bounded preview branch with replaceable WebRTC peers.\n- Provide host-configurable ICE, browser capture assets, and standalone integration guides.","ref":"changelog.html#0-1-0"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}